WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.833
The teal bar runs from nine thirty to ten. Those thirty minutes

00:00:03.833 --> 00:00:07.667
are preparation time. They are not spare space simply because they appear

00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:11.500
before the decision meeting.

00:00:11.733 --> 00:00:15.808
Now compare the amber request from nine forty-five to ten fifteen. It

00:00:15.808 --> 00:00:19.883
takes the last fifteen minutes of preparation and the first fifteen minutes

00:00:19.883 --> 00:00:23.958
of the decision meeting.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:28.425
Keep the supplier slot labelled requested until the approval is verified. Show

00:00:28.425 --> 00:00:32.650
both conflicts when asking for a decision instead of hiding one behind

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:36.875
a calendar change.
